+# [P0] Redis primary quota exhausted — tertiary failover is live; durable quota ledger + alerts required
+
+## Task ID
+`bridge-20261027-redis-quota-ledger`
+
+## Target repository
+`Supremeai-bd/supremeai` (runtime platform concern; tracked on the public `supremeai-open` task board per federation policy).
+
+## Severity
+**P0 — active operational incident.** The primary Upstash Redis instance exceeded its monthly command quota and is in cooldown until 2026-11-01; the secondary is also in cooldown; the tertiary instance is carrying live traffic. There is no evidence of alerting, durable quota accounting, or capacity headroom validation.
+
+## Verified evidence (pulled live via MCP tower, 2026-10-26 16:46 UTC)
+- `redis_rotation_status` →
+  ```json
+  {"autoRotateEnabled": true, "activePrimary": "tertiary",
+   "nextGlobalResetAt": "2026-11-01T00:01:00.000Z",
+   "chain": [
+     {"label": "primary",    "cooldownUntil": "2026-11-01T00:01:00Z", "usage": {"estimatedCommands": 500002, "limit": 500000, "softThreshold": 480000, "softThresholdHit": true}},
+     {"label": "secondary",  "cooldownUntil": "2026-11-01T00:01:00Z", "usage": {"estimatedCommands": 2,     "limit": 500000}},
+     {"label": "tertiary",   "isActivePrimary": true,                 "usage": {"estimatedCommands": 6134,  "limit": 500000}},
+     {"label": "quaternary", "usage": {"estimatedCommands": 1505, "limit": 500000}},
+     {"label": "quinary",    "usage": {"estimatedCommands": 1505, "limit": 500000}},
+     {"label": "tcp-fallback", "usage": {"estimatedCommands": 0}}
+   ]}
+  ```
+- Matches the audit's finding verbatim: primary `500002/500000`, tertiary active, cooldown `2026-11-01T00:01:00Z`.
+
+## Why this blocks production
+- Single-chain-of-rotation fragility: if tertiary burn accelerates (it is now the sole live primary), the platform cascades to quaternary/quinary and then to tcp-fallback with degraded behavior.
+- The audit further notes quota/cooldown state is process-local / best-effort — multi-instance deployments can each think they have headroom and overrun together.
+- ~11 days remain until global reset (2026-11-01); tertiary usage at pull time was 6,134 commands — trajectory unknown because no alerting/history exists.
+
+## Remediation plan
+1. **Alerts**: wire notifications (Telegram ops channel) at 80% / 90% / 96% of `limit` and on any `cooldownUntil` transition for every chain member. Validate against a synthetic threshold crossing.
+2. **Durable shared quota ledger**: persist per-instance counters (and cooldown decisions) in a durable store keyed by instance label so all instances share one truth (the audit's "shared quota ledger" item).
+3. **Command budget review**: identify the top command consumers (cache writes per request, per-token telemetry writes, watchdog polls) and add pipeline batching / sampling to cut burn before reset.
+4. **Capacity validation**: confirm tertiary (and fallbacks) have headroom to carry the full primary load for 11 days; document the failover test result.
+5. **Reset-day plan**: on 2026-11-01 verify rotation returns to primary cleanly (no split-brain double-active).
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+- [ ] Threshold alerts fire in a controlled test
+- [ ] Quota ledger survives an instance restart and is read by all instances
+- [ ] Documented command-burn baseline + reduction actions
+- [ ] Post-reset rotation verified back to primary
+
+## Related orders
+- Audit "SupremeAI সমন্বিত Executive Diagnosis" (2026-10-26), P0 item 7 (Redis quota exhaustion).
